The Advisory Committee shall include:  
- One representative from each trade union;  
- One representative from each employers’ organisation. For each of these groups, one alternate member shall be appointed for each Member State. The members and alternate members of the Advisory Committee shall be appointed in accordance with the rules set out in this Regulation. By 12 June 2008, each Member State must inform the Commission of:  
(a) which courts have the power to issue a European payment order;  
(b) the procedure for reviewing such orders; and  
(c) the methods of communication and the official languages used in these matters. A representative from the European Commission shall attend meetings of the Administrative Commission as an advisor. The rules of the Administrative Commission will be agreed upon by all its members. Decisions on matters of interpretation mentioned in Article 72(a) shall be made according to the voting rules set out in the Treaty and must be published. The Commission of the European Communities will provide secretarial support for the Administrative Commission. The Administrative Commission shall:  
(a) handle all administrative issues and questions about interpretation that arise from this Regulation, the Implementing Regulation, or from any agreement or arrangement made under them;  
(b) do so without limiting the right of authorities, institutions, or individuals to use national legal procedures, courts, or tribunals as provided by national law, this Regulation, or the Treaty.

