The customer has the right to cancel the order during the 14-day period mentioned in Articles 9(2) and 10.  

The right of withdrawal does not apply if:  
- The customer did not ask to start the service or receive the goods during the 14-day period, as required by Articles 7(3) and 8(8);  
- The digital product (like software or music) is not given on a physical medium (like a CD or DVD), and the customer did not give clear permission before the 14 days to start using it;  
- The customer did not clearly agree that they lose the right to cancel when giving permission;  
- The seller did not confirm in writing, as required by Articles 7(2) or 8(7).  

The customer will not be charged or responsible for any money or fees when using the right of withdrawal, unless otherwise stated in Article 13(2) or in this article.  

The right of withdrawal does not affect any other agreements (like payment or delivery) that were made before the withdrawal.

