This Directive applies to services provided by companies based in any EU country.  
However, it does NOT apply to the following types of activities:  
(a) non-economic services that serve the public interest;  
(b) financial services, such as banking, lending, insurance, and reinsurance;  
(c) in the gas sector, services already covered by Directive 2003/55/EC;  
(d) water supply and distribution services, and wastewater treatment services;  
(e) services related to the treatment of waste.  

This Directive does not cover how public interest services are funded, nor does it apply to government financial support given by EU member states — especially in the social sector — as long as such support follows EU competition rules.  
It also does not cover the follow-up to the Commission’s White Paper on public interest services.  

Financial services should be excluded from this Directive because they are already regulated under special EU laws with the same goal: creating a real internal market for services. Therefore, this exclusion should include all financial services, such as banking, lending, insurance, including reinsurance, pension services (both occupational and personal), securities, investment funds, payment services, and investment advice — even if these are listed in Annex I to Directive 2006/48/EC on credit institutions.

